  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Lonidamine is an investigational anticancer agent that has been studied as an antineoplastic and radiosensitizing drug, and it also has antispermatogenic and trypanocidal activity. It is not an approved medicine; it remains an investigational compound with no EMA authorisation.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3836670&quot;>Wikidata Q3836670</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>lonidamine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>L01XX07</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06266&quot;>DB06266</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/39562&quot;>39562</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:50138&quot;>50138</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3836670&quot;>Q3836670</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C15H10Cl2N2O2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>321.157 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
